  "reason": "The RNA-only PCA single-profile baseline is the strongest completed result (0.4849 accuracy, 0.4639 F1), while the image-only ResNet baseline is much weaker, so the main uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved. config_004 keeps rna_only and singleprofile fixed and changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scVI_n200, directly testing whether a learned single-cell representation outperforms PCA. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the promising RNA signal, isolates the representation effect, and avoids confounding profile/aggregation or multimodal fusion changes."
